"""WATCOM 10.0a wcc386 register candidate order (the GiveBestReg FINAL tie-break).

Read directly from wcc386.exe: RegLists[class] table @ va 0x82270 (runtime-coord
0x79918). BuildPossible (0x5db3b) copies RegLists[conf->type_class] into
reg_tree->regs; GiveBestReg iterates that array IN ORDER, and on a full tie
(equal CountRegMoves and equal GivenRegisters membership) the FIRST register in
the list wins. So this order resolves the lowest-level register-choice ties.

hw_reg_set bit layout (OW v1 intel/h/cgi86reg.h; H = the LOW bit of each
byte pair -- confirmed against EMITTED bytes via the frx ground-truth probe,
action.c 2026-07-11: mask 0x40 emits `dh`, 0x8 `bl`, 0x4 `bh`, 0x20 `cl`):
  AH=0 AL=1 BH=2 BL=3 CH=4 CL=5 DH=6 DL=7 SI=8 DI=9 BP=0x400 SP=0x800 (IA-32!)
  E-high: EAX=24 EBX=25 ECX=26 EDX=27 ESI=28 EDI=29
  => EAX=0x1000003 EBX=0x200000c ECX=0x4000030 EDX=0x80000c0
     ESI=0x10000100 EDI=0x20000200 ; AX=0x3 BX=0xc CX=0x30 DX=0xc0

Most important orders:
  class 0x04 (byte) : AL, AH, DL, DH, BL, BH, CL, CH   (== ByteRegs; owp4v1 order,
                      NO high/low swap -- that claim was this table's old bug)
  class 0x08 (word) : AX, DX, BX, CX, SI, DI
  class 0x0f (dword): EAX, EDX, EBX, ECX, ESI, EDI, EBP, ESP  (== DoubleRegs @0x821a8)
  class 0x10 (dword): EAX, EDX, EBX, ECX
  0x13/0x14/0x17    : register PAIRS (long long / double)
"""

